newConnection -- Create a connection to an SCSCP server
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        newConnection (host, port)
  * Inputs:
      * host, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, The name or IP address of
        the host to connect to, with an optional colon followed by the number
        of the port
      * port, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, providing the port number (this argument may be
        omitted)
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note SCSCPConnection: SCSCPConnection,, The
        connection that was established

Description
===========

The port to connect to may be specified either by giving only one argument of
the form host:port or by specifying the second argument. If neither of these is
present, the port defaults to 26133.

See also
========

  * *note SCSCPConnection Thing: SCSCPConnection <== Thing, -- Execute
    computations using SCSCP
  * *note Manipulator SCSCPConnection: Manipulator SCSCPConnection, -- Close an
    SCSCP connection

Ways to use newConnection:
==========================

  * "newConnection(String)"
  * "newConnection(String,String)"
  * "newConnection(String,ZZ)"

